{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>And he called for his son, for Joseph.</b> Because the Holy One, blessed be He, had said to him at his descent to Egypt, 'and Joseph shall place his hand over your eyes' — he called him now. And furthermore, since it was on his account that Jacob came there, it is fitting that he occupy himself with bringing him up." "<b>Place now your hand under my thigh.</b> This was formerly the practice in Israel, similar to clasping hands." "<b>And do with me kindness and truth.</b> This is the fulfilment of pure reciprocal obligation, beyond the strict line of the law, like 'return and bring back your brother with you.' <b>Kindness and truth</b> — and they call it מרצ״י in the vernacular, meaning: you are obligated to bury me, but you are not obligated to trouble yourself to bury me in the land of Canaan; therefore I entreat you, <b>do not bury me, please, in Egypt</b>, to become permanently settled there in burial."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 47, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:08:58.192106321Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}